16 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Infographic divided into three sections explaining PFAS: Section A shows molecular structures of long and short chain PFAS; Section B lists PFAS classes including fluoropolymers, perfluoropolyethers, side-chain fluorinated polymers, and telomers/FASAs with key properties and uses; Section C details surface activity \(enrichment at air-water interface, reduced water surface tension\) and bioaccumulation \(food chain accumulation, protein binding, maternal-fetal exposure\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating proposed mechanisms linking PFAS exposure to adverse assisted reproductive technology \(ART\) outcomes. PFAS exposure leads to accumulation in follicular fluid, affecting the ovarian follicular environment through kisspeptin suppression, steroidogenesis dysfunction, oxidative stress, and chronic inflammation, resulting in reduced oocyte number, poorer embryo quality, poor embryo development, and lower implantation and clinical pregnancy rates.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Four scientific diagrams labeled A to D depict mechanisms of PFAS interference with female reproductive processes: A, suppression of kisspeptin affecting hormonal regulation; B, steroidogenesis dysfunction in ovarian cells; C, mitochondrial oxidative stress via reactive oxygen species; D, chronic uterine inflammation disrupting implantation.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
